# Low Water, Act 2: path-matrix gates as @gate records (SYSTEMS-FULL 19.4; engine
# game/engine/world/gates.mjs). One record per obstacle row of REWORK-PLAN 3.2 (A1 to A9). Each
# pays one page the first time any of its resolved: flags is set, by whichever route.
# Drafted by the systems engineer on 2026-10-17 for the director to correct. Private.
# NOT YET INCLUDED: act2.lwd does not list this file. The director adds `include: gates2.lwd`.
#
# Rules used: only flags set in a winning node (a check's ok node, a fight's win or yield node, the
# node after a successful verb). No fought.* flags. Every flag below was checked by grep for its
# set(...) lines in content/act2/*.lwd. Flags that are also set on a failure, a down or a capture
# were left out, and the comment says so.
#
# Engine note: the engine also pays on load for any flag already set (gates.mjs settle). For that
# reason fennick.bought is not used: Act 1 (act1/quay.lwd) sets it too.
#
# Double pay: some winning nodes already pay a page inline with xp(1): ropewalk.e (A9),
# gasholder.count.ok, gasholder.fennick.paid, gasholder.row.ok (A6). Once this file is included,
# those xp(1) lines pay a second page for the same obstacle. The director picks one.
#
# Daylight page (day.lwd): no gates. Its header says "no checks"; the afternoon calls (Wenna, Pip,
# Merrow, Marrow, the lantern, sleep) are visits with no obstacle and no winning outcome.
#
# Row A10 (which lamps for the gale) is skipped: it is a choice at dawn that every style reaches,
# decided by the lamps Lamb lit on Nights 1 and 2. Nothing is resolved, so there is nothing to pay.
#
# Out of scope, for the director: weigh2.lwd owns a five-route gate of its own (the switch room)
# that is not a row of 3.2. A clean candidate flag is weigh2.in (set only on entry by guise, Hobb,
# FORM LETTER ok, the fight's win, the roof drop ok, the padlock ok). No record is drafted for it.

# Row A1 of REWORK-PLAN 3.2. One flag covers all five routes, because every route ends in a node
# that sets telegram.draft:
#   Fist: ropewalk.fight.door.win / .yield go to ropewalk.draft.read (down goes to the hub).
#   Tongue: Rook's witness (ropewalk.rook.signed) or FORM LETTER ok (ropewalk.rook.form.ok) go to
#     ropewalk.draft.read.
#   Shadow: THE DARK ok (ropewalk.back.ok) goes to ropewalk.draft.read.
#   Hands: GRIP ok on the wire (ropewalk.wire.ok) sets it.
#   Eye: SMALL PRINT ok on the pad (ropewalk.pad.ok) sets it.
# Not used: ropewalk.door_forced (set before the fight, on any outcome).
@gate a2.telegram
name: The 18:30 telegram's draft
resolved: telegram.draft

# GUESS: the matrix names the house, but entry is free (Lamb can knock and be shown in), so the
# obstacle is read as the Trust's ledger page. wages.stopped is also set in hill.dark.caught, the
# fail node of the red THE DARK check in the dark house: Lamb still leaves with the page, but is
# found. If that must not pay, the director adds a route flag to the clean nodes below.
# Row A2 of REWORK-PLAN 3.2. All routes set wages.stopped:
#   Fist: the station fight's win or yield gives the key (hill.key_side), then the side door and
#     hill.ledger.taken.
#   Tongue: Mrs Pellow's errand into the study (hill.ledger.alone), or FORM LETTER ok with Crake
#     (hill.ledger.given).
#   Shadow: the switch thrown, THE DARK ok, then hill.dark.out.
#   Hands: the candle timer (hill.rig.ok, hill.rig.wait), then hill.dark.out.
#   Eye: SMALL PRINT ok on the blind (hill.window.ok).
@gate a2.crake_house
name: Crake's house on the hill
resolved: wages.stopped

# Row A3 of REWORK-PLAN 3.2. Fist: n/a in the matrix.
#   fisk.button: Tongue (brine2.fisk.why after FORM LETTER or CONDOLENCE ok, or the keeper's coat;
#     mole2.fisk.talk.ok; mole2.fisk.clause.ok), Eye (brine2.fisk.read, brine2.fisk.compare: his
#     specification against the struck copy), Shadow (hill.overhear.first, Fisk with Crake), and
#     the GRIP ok at the stove (brine2.fisk.dry). Every setter is a winning node.
#   mole2.wired: Hands (mole2.wire.ok, GRIP ok on the panel plate: the button's wiring).
# Not used: button.tested, the proof of the clause. It is also set on hill.fight.substation.down,
# hill.duct.fail and mole2.test.bright (after the door is lost).
@gate a2.engineer_button
name: The engineer's button
resolved: fisk.button
resolved: mole2.wired

# Row A4 of REWORK-PLAN 3.2. Only two styles have a clean flag:
#   said.quay2_merrow: Tongue (quay2.merrow.ok, CONDOLENCE ok).
#   said.quay2_speak_for_merrow: Tongue (quay2.lugg.ok, THE CHIT ok, Merrow in the cells).
#   quay2.ebb_timed: Eye (quay2.coffin.ok, THE ALMANAC ok, the ebb rowed exactly).
# No clean flag: Fist (quay2.fight.wardens.win / .yield, quay2.wardens.talk.ok,
# quay2.wardens.coat), Shadow (quay2.stow.ok) and Hands (quay2.copper, quay2.cockle.ok,
# quay2.cockle.floor) set only a2.afloat. a2.afloat is also set on quay2.stow.fail (captive),
# quay2.cockle.fail and quay2.coffin.fail, so it is not used. quay2.cockle.mended is also set on
# quay2.cockle.fail. Suggest one new flag set in quay2.row and quay2.stow.ok (both reached only on
# success), listed here once it exists.
@gate a2.spit_boat
name: The boat to the Spit at the second low water
resolved: said.quay2_merrow
resolved: said.quay2_speak_for_merrow
resolved: quay2.ebb_timed

# Row A5 of REWORK-PLAN 3.2. spit.done is set only where the stripping ends in Lamb's favour:
#   Fist: spit.fight.strippers.win / .yield (e.strippers and e.strippers.sneak).
#   Tongue: spit.turn.ok (FORM LETTER ok, the claim read to them).
#   Hands: spit.cut.ok / spit.cut.ride (GRIP ok, the painter cut at the turn).
#   Eye: spit.cargo.told (the claim after SMALL PRINT ok on the stencils; the claim's condition
#     has(spit.cargo) picks this node).
#   Also spit.coat.names (the Lamplighter guise).
# No clean flag for Shadow: spit.watch.ok sets only strippers.named, which is also set in
# spit.captive.hold (Lamb caught and held at the rail). Shadow still earns the i2.names page in
# insights2.lwd from strippers.named.
@gate a2.stripping
name: The stripping of the stranded ships
resolved: spit.done

# Row A6 of REWORK-PLAN 3.2.
#   relics.counted: Fist (gasholder.fight.zealots.win / .yield) and Eye (gasholder.count.ok, SUM ok
#     or the Candlemas eyepiece).
#   gasholder.eye_sealed: Tongue (Ash's accounts, then gasholder.fennick.paid) and Shadow
#     (gasholder.row.ok, UNDERTOW ok under the jar at the Opening).
#   gasholder.bulb_lit: Hands (gasholder.gas.ok, GRIP ok, the Old Bulb on the gasholder's own gas).
# Not used: fennick.bought (Act 1 sets it, so the gate would pay on load for those players). The
# fled and down nodes set only gasholder.zealots_done.
@gate a2.old_bulb
name: The Old Bulb's procession
resolved: relics.counted
resolved: gasholder.eye_sealed
resolved: gasholder.bulb_lit

# GUESS: Tongue, Fist (yield) and Hands converge on hill.test.press, which sets only button.tested
# and hill.test_done; both are also set on hill.fight.substation.down and hill.duct.fail, and
# hill.test_done on hill.fuse.fail. hill.lamb_pressed and hill.crake_pressed are option effects in
# hill.test.dark, reached only on success, but the third option ("Leave it to the engineer") sets
# neither. A new flag in hill.test.press would be cleaner.
# Row A7 of REWORK-PLAN 3.2.
#   struck.subguards: Fist (hill.fight.substation.win). The yield node sets no clean flag.
#   hill.lamb_pressed, hill.crake_pressed: Tongue (hill.sub.fisk, Fisk's authority; hill.sub.form.ok;
#     the Lamplighter guise), Fist (win or yield) and Hands (hill.fuse.ok, hill.fuse.rig: throw it
#     or rig it), all through hill.test.dark.
#   hill.crake_offer: Shadow (hill.duct.ok, BALLAST ok, in by the cable duct).
#   hill.order_restrike: Eye (hill.sub.board, CANDLEMAS ok: the load board through the louvres).
# Not used: hill.watch.write (Eye from the lane) sets only button.tested.
@gate a2.second_switch
name: The substation's second switch
resolved: struck.subguards
resolved: hill.lamb_pressed
resolved: hill.crake_pressed
resolved: hill.crake_offer
resolved: hill.order_restrike

# Row A8 of REWORK-PLAN 3.2.
#   gut2.on_ice: Fist (gut2.fight.ice.win / .yield) and Tongue (gut2.ice.talk.ok, a candidate's
#     speaker in gut2.ice.on.spratt or gut2.ice.on.marrow; also the guild guise).
#   gut2.spratt_deal: Shadow (gut2.ice.sneak.ok, under the ice's noise).
#   gut2.path: Hands (gut2.ice.path.ok, BALLAST ok, salt or ash).
#   gut2.ice_read: Eye (gut2.ice.read.ok, CARBON ok, what froze in on Night 1).
@gate a2.frozen_gutter
name: The frozen gutter
resolved: gut2.on_ice
resolved: gut2.spratt_deal
resolved: gut2.path
resolved: gut2.ice_read

# GUESS: typist.heard is also reached after a failed Shadow check: ropewalk.wall.fail (Hester hears
# the rocking flag), then "Stay where you are" (ropewalk.wall.stay) and the wait. The typing is
# still heard, so the obstacle is resolved, but Lamb was noticed. ropewalk.e also pays xp(1)
# inline (see the header).
# Row A9 of REWORK-PLAN 3.2. One flag, set in the protected moment ropewalk.e, which every route
# reaches through its own lead node:
#   Fist: ropewalk.lead.fist (the back room door, ropewalk.backdoor.ok).
#   Tongue: ropewalk.lead.room (Hester Gannet's front room, through Pip).
#   Shadow: ropewalk.lead.wall (THE DARK ok, through the wall).
#   Hands: ropewalk.lead.grate (the tube's pipe by its frost line, then the grating).
#   Eye: ropewalk.lead.flap (the letter flap, after ropewalk.notice_matched).
@gate a2.sticking_e
name: The sticking e
resolved: typist.heard

# Director, 2026-10-17: the switch room (weigh2), off the matrix, resolved by any way in.
@gate a2.switch_room
name: The Trust's switch room
resolved: weigh2.in
